  "summary": "Malicious code in kepler (npm)",
  "details": "Kepler@1.0.999 declares a dependency \"flag-serial-object-syntax\" as a full URL pointing to hxxps://artifacts[.]yosiroute[.]com/npm/flag-serial-object-syntax instead of a standard npm semver range. The bundled npm-shrinkwrap.json confirms this dependency has install scripts enabled (hasInstallScript: true). When npm installs this package, it will fetch the dependency from the external host, which can serve arbitrary code that executes during installation. The package itself is a minimal 687-byte stub with no real functionality — it exists solely to pull code from the non-standard registry at install time.",
